//! Entries slice — Batch 176 (Plan 176 / Research 214) — the FWHT
//! dtype-native source read: ONE `kernel_opt` rule + 2 riders
//! (`entries_gpu_11` B96 branchless select / `entries_gpu_27` B116
//! upstream width instance), distilled from **ggml-org/llama.cpp**
//! (MIT) at the #29096 merge `6f856c7`
//! (`6f856c70990a1b5a159b0d4b2355160c83c3697b`, merged 2026-09-26) — the
//! rider the idle loop armed on 09-21 and polled 72 times before
//! `merged_at` fired. The PR is the CUDA member of the dtype-native FWHT
//! family: CPU #27779 (merged 09-18, the convert-then-staging CONTRAST),
//! Metal #29094 (merged 09-20, the templated-`src_t` instance + the
//! supported-size refinement), CUDA #29096 (this pin), Metal widths>512
//! #29095 (merged 09-25, the B116 instance rider). The family matters to
//! us beyond the corpus: Hadamard-folded weights are the Bonsai
//! prefill lane (`bonsai2_hadamard` DEFAULT-ON in riir-gpu; the B166
//! in-tree trigger), so every upstream dtype/dispatch decision on this
//! family is league-adjacent intel.
//!
//! Every load-bearing quote re-verified VERBATIM at the merge tree THIS
//! batch (shallow clone at `6f856c7`, the ephemeral-clone law; the
//! review-response commit `6587611` "cuda: use `ggml_cuda_cast` in the
//! FWHT load" is IN the merged form — the pre-study head `65876111e`'s
//! manual cast was superseded, re-graded, no composition change).
//! Category N: the exactness of the F16→F32 widening is the entire
//! legality. Batch 176 / Plan 176 / Research 214.

use crate::domains::kernel_opt::corpus::KernelRule;

/// Data table, not logic -- grows with distillation batches.
#[allow(clippy::too_many_lines)]
pub(super) fn entries() -> Vec<KernelRule> {
    vec![
        // ============================================================
        // -- N: dtype-native transform source read + the shared
        // admission predicate -- the #29096 merge (#29094 Metal twin in
        // the refinement rider; #27779 CPU is the contrast arm). ──────
        KernelRule {
            rule_id: "dtype-native-source-read-with-shared-admission-predicate".to_string(),
            gpu_concept: "A transform kernel whose only input widening is EXACT (F16->F32, f16->f32 -- widening every value without loss) reads the source buffer in its NATIVE dtype and converts AT LOAD, never through a convert-then-staging copy: the source type becomes a template/`src_t` parameter, the load line does the conversion while filling registers (`reg[i] = ggml_cuda_cast<float>(src[i * warp_size + lane]) * scale;` CUDA / `reg[i] = float(src[i*NW + lane])*scale;` Metal), and the staging buffer + its extra pass + its extra full-row traffic simply do not exist. Two decision contents ride with it. (1) THE ADMISSION MUST WIDEN WITH THE KERNEL, and it must be ONE PREDICATE SHARED by supports_op and the dispatch -- verbatim from the PR: 'Without a shared predicate, supports_op could admit an op that ggml_cuda_op_fwht then rejects only after the unconditional same-shape assert has already fired; that gap predates this change (it applies to the existing F32 path too) but this PR is what touches supports_op, so it closes it here.' The shared predicate (`ggml_cuda_op_mul_mat_use_fwht`) carries the WHOLE envelope in one place: op kind + the transform hint (`GGML_HINT_SRC0_IS_HADAMARD`) + the accumulator/output dtype (F32) + the admitted source dtypes (F32 || F16) + contiguity + same-shape. (2) THE RELAXATION IS NARROW -- a mixed-dtype case is admitted ONLY where the transform actually serves it: `if (b->type == GGML_TYPE_F16 && a->type != GGML_TYPE_F16 && !ggml_cuda_op_mul_mat_use_fwht(op)) return false;` -- the generic F32-src0 x F16-src1 path does not exist, 'so admitting a case the FWHT dispatch then declines would fall through to a kernel that does not exist'; a wide admission converts a clean refusal into a wrong-path dispatch (or a crash inside an assert). LEGALITY: the rewrite is exact ONLY because f16->f32 is lossless -- a saturating, rounding, or range-narrowing conversion at load would make this a numerics change requiring the lossy-surface walk (per-family conditional retention), never 'looks fine'; on the exact side it is bit-identical to convert-then-compute (the same values enter the butterfly either way). REGIME: a kernel family serving one exact-widening dtype pair, an admission surface (supports_op / capability query) that dispatch consults, and a hint or similar gate marking the transform-served case. ANTI-REGIME: lossy conversions (the staging copy is then the WRONG shape too, but the point is this rule cannot license it); a dispatch that re-derives the predicate conditions instead of calling the shared fn (drift reintroduces the gap); widths the kernel does not serve (the CPU #27779 contrast converts F16->F32 into a staging buffer -- the avoid-shape this rule exists to eliminate -- AND routes the hint to its own fwht only for F32: the mixed case never reaches a dtype-native kernel there). REFINE RIDER (Metal #29094, merged upstream at the same tree): when the kernel family has a DEVICE-DEPENDENT envelope (threadgroup memory), the size term lives INSIDE the shared predicate -- `ggml_metal_op_mul_mat_use_fwht(op, max_tg_mem)` folds `ggml_metal_fwht_supported_size` in (64-512 simdgroup kernel always; 1024-8192 gated on `n * sizeof(float) <= max_tg_mem`; wider refuses), with the sync contract in-source: 'must stay in sync with the kernel_fwht_<type>_<N> templates in misc.metal' and 'supports_op and the dispatch must ask the same question: an F16 src1 that is admitted but then falls through reaches the generic path, which has no F32 src0 by F16 src1 kernel' -- the envelope-capable backend states the fall-through consequence verbatim where the envelope lives. KINSHIPS: exact-widening-enables-fp16-pv-accumulation (B178) is the family twin -- there the EXACT widening licenses a narrow ACCUMULATOR dtype in an MMA; here it licenses the SOURCE READ dtype + the admission widening; the same lossless-widening legality, different surface. fwht-shuffle-xor-butterfly-register-resident (B96) / fwht-butterfly-staging-ladder-warp-smem-register (B166) / fwht-wide-block-row-per-threadgroup-exchange-ladder (B116) own the transform MECHANISM and width regimes; this owns WHAT TYPE the kernel reads and WHO MAY CALL IT. rht-epilogue-fusion-contract (B105) owns WHERE the transform fuses into a GEMM; fused-transform-quantize-writer (B181) owns the writer layer. Distinct from quantized-source-read rules (those dequant INSIDE the matvec by format -- this is a dtype TEMPLATE over an already-decodable binary format, no format knowledge in the kernel). Consumer context: Hadamard-folded weights are the Bonsai prefill lane (bonsai2_hadamard DEFAULT-ON in riir-gpu) -- an F16-activation fold source read halves the activation-side load bytes for the fold, the same traffic axis the upstream family serves. Source: ggml-org/llama.cpp @ 6f856c70990a1b5a159b0d4b2355160c83c3697b (#29096, merged 2026-09-26) -- ggml/src/ggml-cuda/fwht.cu L5 (`template <int N, typename T>`), L26 (the cast-at-load line), L101-110 (`ggml_cuda_op_mul_mat_use_fwht` body), L118-130 (the `<float>`/`<half>` impl switch), ggml/src/ggml-cuda/ggml-cuda.cu L5214 (the narrow refusal); Metal twin #29094 @ the same tree -- ggml/src/ggml-metal/kernels/misc.metal L380 (`device const src_t * src`), L405 (the load), L507-528 (the `kernel_fwht_f32_N`/`kernel_fwht_f16_N` template sets, same host names), ggml/src/ggml-metal/ggml-metal-common.cpp L13-33 (supported_size + the Metal shared predicate + both sync comments); contrast #27779 @ the same tree -- ggml/src/ggml-cpu/ggml-cpu.c L1263 (the hint routes to the convert-then-staging CPU fwht); tests/test-backend-ops.cpp (6 new F16 cases: 64/128/256/512 single-row + 128x32 + 256x512 many-rows). Batch 176 / Plan 176 / Research 214. (Batch 192 note: upstream #29602 @ 18bbc46 moved 512 to the threadgroup form — the boundary is now 64-256 simdgroup / 512-8192 tg-gated; read widths from the tree, not from this rider.)".to_string(),
            ref_shape: "// naive: the transform accepts F32 only, so an F16 activation is\n// bulk-converted into a staging buffer first -- a full extra pass over\n// the row set, and the mixed-dtype case is refused far from the kernel\n// (or admitted and crashed on).\nfn fwht_staged(src: &[f32], dst: &mut [f32], scale: f32) {\n    for (d, s) in dst.iter_mut().zip(src.iter()) {\n        *d = s * scale; // the kernel only ever sees F32\n    }\n    butterfly(dst);\n}\n\nfn convert_f16_to_f32_staging(src_f16: &[u16]) -> Vec<f32> {\n    src_f16.iter().map(|b| half_to_f32(*b)).collect() // the staging copy\n}\n\nfn half_to_f32(_bits: u16) -> f32 {\n    0.0\n}\n\nfn butterfly(_buf: &mut [f32]) {}".to_string(),
            opt_pattern: "// optimized: the source type is a template parameter; the conversion\n// rides the register fill. ONE predicate governs admission AND dispatch.\nfn fwht<T: HalfOrF32>(src: &[T], dst: &mut [f32], scale: f32) {\n    let lane = lane_id();\n    let mut reg = [0.0f32; NE];\n    for (i, r) in reg.iter_mut().enumerate() {\n        // cast-at-load: f16->f32 is EXACT, so this is bit-identical to\n        // convert-then-compute -- without the staging buffer or the pass\n        *r = src[i * WARP + lane].to_f32() * scale;\n    }\n    butterfly_regs(&mut reg, lane);\n    dst.copy_from_slice(&reg);\n}\n\n/// THE shared predicate: supports_op and the dispatch call THIS, never a\n/// re-derived copy -- a predicate split admits what the dispatch then\n/// rejects after its unconditional same-shape assert has fired.\nfn mul_mat_use_fwht(a_is_f32: bool, b_ty: Ty, hint: Hint, contiguous: bool, same_shape: bool) -> bool {\n    hint == Hint::Src0IsHadamard\n        && a_is_f32\n        && matches!(b_ty, Ty::F32 | Ty::F16) // the EXACT-widening pair only\n        && contiguous\n        && same_shape\n}\n\n/// The relaxation stays NARROW: refuse the mixed case UNLESS the\n/// transform serves it -- the generic F32-src0 x F16-src1 kernel does\n/// not exist, and a too-wide admission falls through to it.\nfn supports_op_mixed_dtype(a_ty: Ty, b_ty: Ty, op: Op) -> bool {\n    !(b_ty == Ty::F16 && a_ty != Ty::F16 && !op.use_fwht())\n}\n\nenum Ty {\n    F32,\n    F16,\n}\n\nenum Hint {\n    Src0IsHadamard,\n    None,\n}\n\nstruct Op {\n    use_fwht: bool,\n}\n\nimpl Op {\n    fn use_fwht(&self) -> bool {\n        self.use_fwht\n    }\n}".to_string(),
        },
    ]
}
